# ── Provisioning ────────────────────────────────────────────────────

@Given "^an existing counterparty keyword is available$"
    Given build request as user 'maker@example.com'
    And set query parameter 'page' to '1'
    And set query parameter 'size' to '10'
    When get from path '/refdata/counterparties'
    Then response status code is '200'
    And store response field 'data.content[0].counterpartyCode' as 'counterpartyKeywordFromList'

@Given "^an existing counterparty id is available$"
    Given build request as user 'maker@example.com'
    And set query parameter 'page' to '0'
    And set query parameter 'size' to '10'
    When get from path '/refdata/counterparties'
    Then response status code is '200'
    And store response field 'data.content[0].id' as 'counterpartyIdFromList'

# ── Make API calls ───────────────────────────────────────────────────

@When "^retrieves counterparties with paging parameters$"
    Given build request as user 'maker@example.com'
    And set query parameter 'page' to '0'
    And set query parameter 'size' to '10'
    When get from path '/refdata/counterparties'
    And attach the response body to the report

@When "^searches counterparties by keyword$"
    Given build request as user 'maker@example.com'
    And set query parameter 'keyword' from stored variable 'counterpartyKeywordFromList'
    And set query parameter 'page' to '0'
    And set query parameter 'size' to '10'
    When get from path '/refdata/counterparties'
    And attach the response body to the report

@When "^retrieves counterparty detail by id$"
    Given build request as user 'maker@example.com'
    And set path parameter 'id' from stored variable 'counterpartyIdFromList'
    When get from path '/refdata/counterparties/{id}'
    And attach the response body to the report

# ── Assertions ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────

@Then "^counterparties list should be retrieved successfully$"
    Then the 'counterparties list' should be 'retrieved' successfully

@Then "^counterparties search results should match requested keyword$"
    Then the 'counterparties search' should be 'retrieved' successfully
    And response body contains a key 'data.content[0].counterpartyCode' with stored variable 'counterpartyKeywordFromList'

@Then "^counterparty detail should be retrieved successfully$"
    Then the 'counterparty detail' should be 'retrieved' successfully
    And response body contains a key 'data.id' with stored variable 'counterpartyIdFromList'
